<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jeongjo of Joseon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1752–1800</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as King Jeongjo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jeongjo was the 22nd king of Joseon <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, ruling from 1776 to 1800. The son of the executed Crown Prince Sado, he continued his grandfather Yeongjo's policy of balancing court factions, founded the royal library <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gyujanggak">Kyujanggak</a> to promote scholarship and built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hwaseong-fortress">Hwaseong Fortress</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suwon">Suwon</a>. His reign is seen as the last high point of the dynasty.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jeongjo-of-joseon.jpg" alt="Jeongjo of Joseon" width="313" height="500" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aitadzh Z · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%87oson_Kral%C4%B1_Conqco.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
